@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] mila-porsche-only-transport
Mila MUST reach a deployment only through its Porsche SSH gateway running
`--json` commands, plus the HTTPS trust document fetch. It MUST NOT call
Marshall HTTP APIs or hold account authority itself (ADR-0220).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] mila-strict-host-certificates
Mila MUST accept a host only with a current Ed25519 host certificate from the
pinned CA naming the deployment's management host, checked during key
exchange before user authentication. There MUST be no trust-on-first-use, no
unsigned fallback, and a changed CA, host or zone MUST be refused (ADR-0228).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] mila-device-key-custody
Each deployment MUST get its own P-256 device key. iOS, Android and signed
macOS private keys MUST stay in the Secure Enclave or Android Keystore, and
Windows keys MUST stay in a non-exportable CNG provider (the TPM's Platform
Crypto Provider, or the software key storage provider where there is no TPM).
Only the explicitly compiled `MILA_SOFTWARE_KEYS` macOS development build may
use an owner-only software key; release and iOS builds MUST refuse software
custody. Private keys never cross the platform channel; the Linux test key
MUST be owner-only and a readable key file MUST be refused. Keys, signatures
and tokens MUST NOT be logged.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture] mila-pure-core
`native Rust core` and `native transport` MUST NOT import retired client.
Protocol decoding, routing and state machines live in `mila_core`.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] mila-links-navigate-only
Following an `overalls://` link MUST only navigate. It MUST NOT send a
command, add a deployment or approve anything, and links to an unknown or
signed-out deployment MUST NOT open a deployment page (ADR-0221).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol] mila-mutation-once
A mutation MUST be submitted at most once with its client request id; any
uncertainty MUST be resolved by polling `request show`, never by resubmitting.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol;security] mila-vm-shape-bounds
Every native machine create and resize boundary MUST accept only the shared VM
shape limits: CPU 1..=256, memory 256..=4,194,304 MiB, and disk 1..=500 GiB.
Values outside these ranges MUST be rejected before crossing the platform FFI
boundary.
